      "id": "/content/3DEfbEapcms4kBA2agQjtnQkutu",
      "title": "Governing MCP in Kiro: curating one approved set of servers for your team",
      "description": "By default, every developer can add any MCP server they want, leaving teams with an inconsistent, unvetted mix of tools. This article is a hands-on walkthrough of Kiro's MCP governance: how an admin curates an approved registry of servers, hosts it, and wires it into the Kiro profile so the whole org runs one consistent, vetted set. It uses three real servers to show each pattern end to end, from writing the registry file to seeing the governed servers in action.",
      "url": "https://builder.aws.com/content/3DEfbEapcms4kBA2agQjtnQkutu",
